* ============================================================================
* workspace_ram_hydrate.dts -- memo -> RAM hydration (owner lane step 2,
* 2026-08-11): WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO RAM copies the posture's tables and
* native CDX files from their DISK homes into the mounted RAM VFS (through
* xbase::ramfs streams -- never std::filesystem, which would land on real
* disk while claiming RAM), then loads the posture with its roots re-pointed
* at RAM via the DTSHEMA 3 self-location mechanism. LMDB is not hydrated
* (owner rule "lmdb only for disks"; ramfs.hpp: LMDB must mmap a real OS
* file). Memo-sidecar hydration is chartered with the Part B regeneration
* (no MCC table carries a memo field yet).
*
* The hydration is TIMED and prints a measured line -- first measure
* 2026-08-11 (build 14:59:07): 24 file(s), 92139 B in 94.2 ms, and the VDISK
* census independently agreed byte-for-byte (92139 B / 24 files).
*
* Self-contained: saves its own v3 source posture from mcc_x64 first, so it
* never depends on hand-made catalog rows. VDISK UNMOUNT at the end is the
* DISMISS exit of the two-exit close: all RAM files dropped, disk untouched.
*
* Run: DO workspace_ram_hydrate  |  regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_RAM
* Markers: HYD_T1 (STUDENTS row readable from the RAM-resident copy).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-RAM-HYDRATE-BEGIN"

* --- author the source posture (v3, self-locating) from the disk env --------
* DO x64, not bare SETPATHs: measured 2026-08-11 -- under SETPATH DBF/INDEXES
* alone (no LMDB slot), LOAD mcc_x64 attached ZERO CDX orders and the saved
* posture recorded index=none for all 11 (payload 1223 B vs 1286 B, the 63 B
* being 'none' replacing eleven .cdx names). The x64 CDX lane needs its LMDB
* slot; DO x64 carries all three. The 13-vs-24 hydrated-file variance between
* the first regression run and the hand run was THIS, not a hydrator defect.
* AMENDED 2026-08-28. 'WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64' is why this spec could not be
* bracketed: mcc_x64 is a posture FILE in the PRODUCTION workspaces directory,
* so the spec read production to build its own fixture. Under the AIF-078 L2
* bracket the WORKSPACES slot points at a scratch root and that file is absent.
* It now builds its own posture, like every self-bootstrapping spec here.
* STUDENTS stays in AREA 8 because mcc_x64 held it there and HYD_T1 reads
* SELECT 8 -- the FIXTURE changes, the PROOF does not. Two areas rather than
* thirteen; the count was never the claim, hydration of a readable row is.
DO x64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SELECT 1
USE DEPT
SELECT 8
USE STUDENTS
WORKSPACE SAVE ram_hydrate_src MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- mount the RAM VFS and hydrate ------------------------------------------
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD ram_hydrate_src MEMO RAM

* --- residency + readability proof ------------------------------------------
VDISK STATUS
* CORRECTED 2026-08-28, SAME DAY, AFTER A FALSE GREEN. This assertion used to
* address the table by SLOT (SELECT 8), and the amendment above kept slot 8 on
* the reasoning that the old fixture held STUDENTS there. THAT REASONING WAS
* VOID: R130 says a posture's AREA numbers are KEYS, NOT ADDRESSES, and the
* load prints so -- tables land at slots 0..N-1. The old fixture only worked
* because mcc_x64 restored THIRTEEN areas, so slot 8 coincidentally held
* STUDENTS. With a small posture SELECT 8 reaches NOTHING -- and the marker
* still printed .T., because a marker over a closed area does not error, it
* picks a side (see claude/FINDING_MARKER_OVER_A_CLOSED_AREA_PICKS_A_SIDE.md).
* ADDRESSING BY NAME SURVIVES RELOCATION, which is why workspace_memo and
* workspace_load_shortfall stayed sound through the same change.
SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
? "HYD_T1_students_in_ram:" + (SID >= 1)

FORMULA "WS-RAM-HYDRATE-END"

* --- the dismiss exit: drop everything, restore the disk environment --------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
